<title>UK: John Lewis weekly UK store sales up 10.9% y/y.</title>
<headline>John Lewis weekly UK store sales up 10.9% y/y.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The John Lewis Partnership said on Friday its UK department store sales for the week to August 31 were up 10.9 percent year on year.</p>
<p>For the five weeks to August 31, department store sales were up 18.2 percent year on year.  </p>
<p>Total sales, including those from the Waitrose supermarket chain, rose 10.5 percent year on year.</p>
<p>For the five-week period, sales were up 12.9 percent.</p>
<p>-- Mike Peacock, London Newsroom 44 171 542 2774</p>
</text>
